📄 Day 37: Read a Text File and Count Words, Lines, and Characters

📌 Project Overview

This is my Day 37 Python project, where I built a program that reads a .txt file and analyses its contents.

The program asks the user for a file name, reads the file, and calculates the number of lines, words, and characters. It also counts non-empty lines, finds the longest word, and identifies the most common word.

If the requested file does not exist, the program displays a friendly error message instead of crashing.

This project helped me practise file handling, string methods, lists, dictionaries, exception handling, and basic text analysis.

🎯 Features

✅ Ask the user for a text file name.

✅ Read the entire file using file.read().

✅ Count the total number of lines.

✅ Count the total number of words.

✅ Count characters, including spaces and line breaks.

✅ Handle missing files using try/except FileNotFoundError.

✅ Handle empty files without crashing.

✅ Count non-empty lines.

✅ Find the longest word.

✅ Find the most common word.

✅ Ignore letter case when counting word frequencies.

✅ Remove selected punctuation from the beginning and end of words.

✅ Check multiple files until the user enters q or Q.

